WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.897 --> 00:00:09.390
Companies are complicated.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.980
Investment is tricky.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.580
Predictions are hard to make,
especially about the future.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.590
What's needed are
local guides who

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.230
try to point investors
in the right direction.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:22.830
We have them in the form
of securities analysts.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.710
These professionals typically
work for brokers, investment

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.240
banks, and fund managers.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.080
They do statistical analysis
and talk to company bosses.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.960
Recently, they seem to
have been in retreat.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.820
What's gone wrong for them?

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.550
First, regulation
has tightened up.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.500
Customers have decided
fewer analysts are needed.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.310
Second, investment is changing.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:48.870
Customers, who are mostly active
managers, are in retreat too.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.200
Third, the focus of big
business is shifting.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.000
Companies are beginning
to see a purpose

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.340
broader than shareholder value.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.560
Many analysts
specialise in valuations

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.450
based on next year's profits.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:03.960
That's an important
skill, but a narrow one.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.510
Are securities analysts doomed?

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:09.930
Are analysts now as obsolete
as diesel cars or cassette

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:10.770
players?

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.330
Let's consider each challenge.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.600
The regulatory hit comes
from Mifid II in the EU.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.750
Commentators have likened
it to the triffid,

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.740
a fictional man-eating plant.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.890
Before Mifid II, fund
managers routed their trades

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.140
to a broker to
execute on the market.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.750
In return, brokers
charged commissions

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.400
that included the
cost of research

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.440
received by the fund manager.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.830
Mifid II required fund
managers to disclose this cost

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.090
to their clients.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:38.760
Embarrassed, they decided
they needed less of it.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.250
The trend is spilling
over into the US.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.730
Other changes are thinning the
ranks of securities analysts.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.850
Index funds, which passively
track market benchmarks,

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.410
are growing fast.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:53.460
PwC forecasts index funds will
account for half the US total

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.560
by 2025.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.230
But Lex thinks reports of
the death of the securities

00:01:58.230 --> 00:01:59.850
analysts are exaggerated.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:00.900
Here's why.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.790
Analysts blind to
societal change

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.190
are as doomed as any
other professionals.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.250
Those who adapt are not.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.930
They can calculate discounts
on oil and gas reserves

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.360
due to climate
change, for example.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.870
Index funds have made smaller
inroads than worriers imagined.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:20.370
And their share of the US stock
market is only 13 per cent.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.220
Moreover, part of the
justification for index funds

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.500
is misleading.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.490
They are certainly
low cost and may

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.680
appear to remove human error.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.850
But in reality, index compilers
can still make bad choices.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.950
They could trap
investors in weak sectors

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.550
during downturns when it could
increase financial instability.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:42.240
Finally, people will
always need other people

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.820
to study the numbers
behind investment.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.970
UK and US brokers may
require fewer analysts.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.550
Other employers may want more.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:54.420
Data from the CFA Institute show
demand to take its tough exams

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:59.090
is rising sharply in Asia
and is steady elsewhere.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.230
The securities analysts is dead.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.390
Long live the
securities analyst.

